@startuml sc-moves-layers
!include ../../themes/proveo.puml
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam defaultTextAlignment left
title StarChess · Classical geometry and native admission boundaries

package "packages/starchess-core" {
  component "board/moves.ts\nscMovesFrom / scMovesFor\nisScMoveShape" as SCM <<app>>
  component "board/placement.ts\nattacksSquare / clearRay" as BRD <<app>>
  component "board/siege.ts\nisTankSiegedAfterB" as SIEGE <<app>>
  component "board/mines.ts\nmine targets, not occupancy" as MIN <<app>>
  component "board/vision.ts\ntank / siege footprint" as VIS <<app>>
  component "rules/validation.ts\nassertClassicalBaseline\nassertNativeClassicalDependencies" as VAL <<error>>
  component "rules/nativeClassical.ts\nnativeClassicalChecks\nmatchedMarineDouble" as OWN <<app>>
  component "rules/planning-intents.ts\nclassicalActorAt / knownAppendFailure" as PUBLIC <<app>>
  component "commands/queue-action.ts\naddScAction / removeScAction" as QACT <<async>>
  component "ai/adjutant.ts\nclassical candidates" as BRAIN <<app>>
}
package "apps/starchess" {
  component "LiveStarChessBoard\nonSquareClick" as LIVE <<app>>
  component "presentation/board/hooks/useBoardInput.ts\nviewer occupancy / selection" as INPUT <<app>>
  component "MatchStore / matchReducer\nQUEUE_ACTION / SUBMIT_TURN" as STORE <<async>>
}
cloud "chess.js\nSquare type only" as CJS <<cloud>>

SCM ARROW_MAIN BRD : leap / ray geometry
SCM ARROW_OPTIONAL SIEGE : move-generation mode
SCM ARROW_OPTIONAL MIN : Marine diagonal targets
SCM ARROW_OPTIONAL VIS : tank 5x5 / siege 9x9
BRAIN ARROW_MAIN SCM : scMovesFor
PUBLIC ARROW_MAIN SCM : known-board shape law
LIVE ARROW_MAIN INPUT : click origin / destination
INPUT ARROW_MAIN SCM : highlights from viewer map
INPUT ARROW_QUEUE STORE : SELECT_SQUARE / SET_LEGAL_DESTS\nSET_PENDING_PROMOTION / QUEUE_ACTION
STORE ARROW_MAIN QACT : same native gates as scripts
QACT ARROW_MAIN VAL : admission and retained-C dependencies
VAL ARROW_MAIN OWN : own units / own siege / own queue
OWN ARROW_MAIN SCM : mandatory shape or matched Marine double
OWN ARROW_MAIN BRD : private own-dependency bookkeeping
STORE ARROW_OPTIONAL CJS : no chess.js legality oracle

note right of OWN
  Own B replacements determine C's effective
  type, even over an allied old occupant.
  Public planning helpers retain their earlier
  precedence, rather than supplying this guard.
end note
note bottom of VAL
  Native shape validation rejects bad vectors
  without using a path-clearance test.
  The resolver still discovers hidden contact,
  so legal geometric attempts remain valid.
end note
note bottom of QACT
  Promotion and siege validation follow the
  effective type, not a replaced predecessor.
  Shifted last-rank promotion still fails at End,
  rather than moving that error into admission.
end note
note bottom of INPUT
  Board input hides unseen enemy pieces
  before it asks for move highlights.
  Native command admission remains authoritative,
  so the UI does not introduce another rule set.
end note
note right of STORE
  No Coach BoardMoveProvider route.
  Specials use the same QUEUE_ACTION path.
end note
note top of STORE
  PromotionModal selects the last-rank unit.
  Timeout / End may flush the queen default.
end note
note bottom of CJS
  Chess.js excludes adjacent kings, whereas
  StarChess deliberately permits the CC duel.
  Its move oracle would therefore reject
  a supported native interaction.
end note
note right of MIN
  Move generation includes Marine diagonals
  when a hostile mine supplies a target.
  Native resolution distinguishes attack clearing
  from lethal movement onto an armed mine.
end note
note right of SCM
  Hoverbike: L (1,2) or (2,1).
  CC: adjacent step, no castling or self-check.
end note
note left of SCM
  Mecha: diagonal; Tank: orthogonal.
  BattleShip: either nonzero ray; no no-op.
end note
note top of SCM
  Marine: forward push or diagonal attack.
  Double band: White <=2, Black >=7.
  Back-rank deployment keeps positional rights.
end note
note top of MIN
  Marine pushes never capture forward.
  No en passant; blockers truncate the walk.
end note
note bottom of SIEGE
  Sieged move generation emits cross targets,
  with no own aims and no diagonal shelling.
  Native resolution owns ray contact, visible
  empty-target shelling and mine clearing,
  without relocating the packed Tank.
end note
note top of OWN
  Insertion and resulting C states retain
  separate geometry, siege and promotion checks.
  Later replacements cannot erase a failure
  already present when C entered the queue.
end note
note top of VIS
  Enemy CC aims carry dropsAtResolve.
  UI and scripts filter those highlights.
end note
note left of PUBLIC
  No new candidate-domain contract.
  No private helper on root or planning-v1.
end note
note top of QACT
  No queue-time checkmate or path oracle.
  Gas and B/F generation stay separate.
end note
@enduml
